  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Start here",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 16,
        "h": 9
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n### Alert-development workbench\n\nThis dashboard exists to help you find and validate Graphite metric paths\nbefore turning them into alert rules. It is deliberately plain.\n\n**How to use it**\n\n1. Pick your GHES host from the **host** dropdown at the top.\n2. Look at the **Discovery** row first. Those panels use wildcards and will\n   show you what actually exists in your metric tree. If a panel is empty,\n   your namespace differs from the assumed `collectd.<host>.*` layout --\n   fix the query here before going further.\n3. In the **Alert candidates** row, each panel is a single series, which is\n   what an alert rule needs. Panel edit -> copy the `target` string.\n4. Build the rule at **Alerting -> Alert rules -> New alert rule**, and paste\n   the target there. **Replace `$host` with a literal hostname** -- alert\n   rules cannot resolve dashboard template variables.\n\n**Thresholds shown here are placeholders.** Set the panel time range to 7 or\n30 days and look at how each metric actually behaves before you commit to a\nnumber. Disk trends slowly; load spikes constantly. They want very different\npending periods.\n"
      },
      "transparent": false
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "If nothing renders",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 9
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n**If the Discovery panels are empty**, your metric namespace is different.\nCommon variations:\n\n- `collectd.<host>.` vs `<host>.` vs `servers.<host>.`\n- Mount naming: `df-data-user` (for `/data/user`), `df-root`, `df-data`\n- Newer collectd: `df-<mount>.percent_bytes-free` instead of `df_complex-*`\n- Aggregated CPU: `aggregation-cpu-average.cpu-idle`\n\nUse the Graphite query editor's metric tree browser (click each segment) to\nfind the real paths, then fix the panels. That browsing *is* the point of\nthis dashboard.\n"
      },
      "transparent": false
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Discovery -- what actually exists",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "All filesystems: free bytes (wildcard)",
      "description": "Wildcard across every mount. Use this to learn your real mount names, then hardcode the one you care about in an alert rule.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "graphite",
        "uid": "${DS_GRAPHITE}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "target": "aliasByNode(collectd.$host.df-*.df_complex-free, 2)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "graphite",
            "uid": "${DS_GRAPHITE}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
